# plans/pr-review-boards-2026-09-22-phase-4-plan.md P4-T07 (FEA-26) · UX-SPEC.md §Board "The
# other three dialogs" (Board settings › Schedules) · KEYMAP.md §Dialog > BoardSettings ·
# TESTING-HARNESS.md §11 (the
# `section` and row-editor fields) — on a Reviews board, `n` in the Schedules section starts
# from the GitHub review starter.
#
# The `reviews` preset (§4) seeds the context's Reviews board, and the daemon advertises
# `schedules`, so the rail reads General, Backend, Columns, Schedules: three `tab` from the
# General the dialog opens on in a fresh session. `n` there is the new-schedule form, and on a
# Reviews board it is pre-filled with the starter — the name `GitHub reviews` and
# `fleet_core::schedule::STARTER_PROMPT_GITHUB_REVIEWS`.
#
# The form's values are read through the one row-scoped editor a row mounts on `⏎`, which is the
# only place a Board settings text row can be read back (§11): `dialog.fields[1]` is named after
# the row. The rows run Name, Enabled, Repeat, Every, Timeout, Provider, Model, Effort, Mode,
# Prompt — Once at is hidden while Repeat is `every` — so Prompt is nine `j` below Name. `esc` in
# an open editor reverts the row and stays in the form.
#
# Nothing is saved: `^s` would create a schedule, and that is FEA-26's gpui tests' business. The
# fields are read with `assert`, never `await`: typing and editors do not notify `AppState` (§11).
#
# Headless: virtual-lane only, because of its `shot`. Every other line runs headless (§7).
fixture: reviews
await idle 30000
key g p
await hub_tab == Prs 15000
key tab
await key_contexts[2] == "Board" 20000
await lists.board.rows[0].label == "Pending review" 20000

# `,` opens Board settings on this board; the rail's fourth section is Schedules.
key ,
await dialog.name == BoardSettings 15000
assert dialog.fields[0].name == "section" && dialog.fields[0].value == "General"
key tab tab tab
assert dialog.fields[0].value == "Schedules"
assert key_contexts[0] == "Dialog" && key_contexts[1] == "BoardSettings"

# `n` is the starter form. Its Name row carries the starter's name.
key n
key enter
assert key_contexts[1] == "BoardSettingsEditing"
assert dialog.fields[1].name == "name" && dialog.fields[1].value == "GitHub reviews"
key escape
assert key_contexts[1] == "BoardSettings" && dialog.fields[0].value == "Schedules"

# And its Prompt row carries the starter's prompt.
key j j j j j j j j j
key enter
assert dialog.fields[1].name == "prompt"
assert dialog.fields[1].value ~= "^List every open pull request where my review is requested, directly or through one of my teams, with gh search prs --review-requested=@me"
assert dialog.fields[1].value ~= "use its updatedAt as the requested time and github as the source label\\.$"
key escape
assert key_contexts[1] == "BoardSettings"
shot schedules-starter
quit
